  "confidence": 0.8,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D25", "D26", "D27"],
      "pins": ["D25.2", "D26.2", "D27.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0151", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "The anodes of D25, D26, and D27 are tied together on net /NET0151, but that net contains no power or other connection. D25/D26/D27 are LEDs whose cathodes are connected through resistors to CM4 LED sink outputs.",
      "expected": "The common LED anodes should be connected to a supply rail such as +3V3 so that the CM4 active-low/open-drain LED outputs (Ethernet_nLED2/3 and PI_nLED_Activity) can sink current and light the LEDs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"37\") (name \"/NET0151\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D25\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D26\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D27\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"D25\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"K\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"R27\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The Ethernet and activity LEDs cannot light because their anodes are floating; status indication for Ethernet link/activity and Pi activity is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U19", "U23"],
      "pins": ["U19.4", "U19.5", "U23.4", "U23.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Both isolated CAN transceivers have their primary and secondary ground pins connected to the same GND net: U19 pin 4 (GND1) and pin 5 (GND2) are on GND, and U23 pin 4 (GND1) and pin 5 (GND2) are also on GND.",
      "expected": "For an isolated CAN transceiver, GND1 and GND2 should be separate ground domains (with isolated VCC1/VCC2 as needed) to maintain galvanic isolation between the board-side CAN logic and the field/CAN bus side.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver (`U11`/companion)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U19\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U19\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U23\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U23\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN transceivers are not galvanically isolated as intended; the isolation barrier is shorted, so CAN bus ground faults or ground loops are not isolated from the board ground.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows a clear open connection: D25-D27 LED anodes are tied together on /NET0151 but not connected to any supply, so the Ethernet/activity LEDs cannot light. A secondary concern is that the isolated CAN transceivers have GND1 and GND2 tied to common GND, which defeats the stated CAN isolation."
}

